# Secrets and key material
# ·················
# This repository is public and carries no secret key material by design.
# These patterns stay broad anyway: a false positive costs one `git add -f`, a false
# negative is unrecoverable once pushed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.secrets.*
*.local.*
# Backstop against committing internal working documents.
*.private.*
*.internal.*

# Editors and OS
# ·················
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Corpus scope
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file excludes no specification. Publishing one is an addition, and
# nothing else moves: a corpus proof certifies the documents its rules domain is
# made of (rules-domain/1 Section 13.3), so no existing proof is disturbed.
#
# What is published is what `normative/index.md` lists. That index is the
# authority on the corpus's extent — not this file.

